WEBVTT

00:03:27.119 --> 00:03:30.539
when you feel like the ground
on which you’re standing might not hold?

00:03:30.957 --> 00:03:32.250
In the world of today,

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.794
filled with political instability,

00:03:34.794 --> 00:03:39.298
climate disasters, where our spaces
are constantly ravaged and threatened,

00:03:39.298 --> 00:03:41.175
how do you create a sense of home?

00:03:41.509 --> 00:03:44.262
In 2020 when the pandemic hit,

00:03:44.262 --> 00:03:45.263
we all felt --

00:03:45.263 --> 00:03:47.974
or at least those of us
lucky enough to have homes --

00:03:47.974 --> 00:03:49.058
we all went inside,

00:03:49.058 --> 00:03:50.810
and that became our safe space.

00:03:51.185 --> 00:03:53.688
The outside world became the threat:

00:03:53.688 --> 00:03:54.855
the air, the people.

00:03:54.855 --> 00:03:56.857
This invisible monster was outside.

00:03:57.316 --> 00:03:59.568
But as long as you were
tucked in your bubble,

00:03:59.568 --> 00:04:00.569
you were safe.